THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

This repository vendors its dependencies rather than fetching them, so every
third-party component ships with its own license beside the code it covers:

  vendor/sqlite/      SQLite amalgamation — public domain (LICENSE.md)
  vendor/libsodium/   libsodium — ISC (LICENSE)
  vendor/json/        nlohmann/json — MIT (LICENSE.md)
  vendor/stb/         stb single-file libraries — MIT / public domain (LICENSE.md)
  vendor/blake3/      BLAKE3 — CC0 (LICENSE-CC0.txt)
  vendor/icons/       Lucide icons — ISC (LICENSE-lucide.txt)
  vendor/fonts/       Inter, Source Serif, Space Grotesk, Lato, JetBrains Mono —
                      SIL Open Font License (OFL-*.txt); Font Awesome Free
                      (LICENSE.md)

  demo-assets/        The Cat Colony demo photographs, from cataas.com. The
                      colony itself is fictional: fifty invented cats with
                      invented biographies, shipped so the application has a
                      real dataset to open on first run and so no example in
                      this repository is ever a real person.
